/-!
# Rigidity of 2-morphisms of the small étale ringed topos of an algebraic space

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf
site `B`.  Stacks 04KK asserts that the morphism of small étale ringed topoi of Stacks 03G8 has
no non-trivial 2-endomorphisms: a 2-morphism from `(f_{small}, f^♯)` to itself, in the sense of
Stacks 04IC, is the identity.

The argument is the one in the source, read through the chart correspondence of Stacks 03G8.
A 2-morphism is a transformation of the direct-image functors compatible with the structure map,
and affine étale charts of `Y` detect it (Stacks 04JS).  Over an affine chart `V` the sections of
the direct image of a sheaf `𝓖` on the small étale site of `X` are, naturally in `𝓖`, the
homomorphisms out of a *single* sheaf: the subsheaf of a product of copies of `𝒪_X` generated by
the presheaf of chart morphisms over `f` with lower chart `V`.  So the transformation is
precomposition with an endomorphism of that sheaf, the compatibility with the structure map says
that the endomorphism fixes each coordinate, and the coordinates are jointly monic because `V` is
affine.  Hence the endomorphism, and so the 2-morphism, is the identity.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallEtaleRingedToposHom_twoMorphism_eq_id`: **Stacks 04KK** — every
  2-endomorphism of the morphism of small étale ringed topoi induced by a morphism of algebraic
  spaces is the identity.

## Implementation notes

The presheaf of chart morphisms over `f` with lower chart `V` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartFiber`.  Its sections over a chart `U` of `X` are exactly the
diagrams of charts of Stacks 03G3 with upper chart `U` and lower chart `V`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartFiberOfBaseChangeArrow` identifies them with the morphisms from
`U` into the cartesian base change `X ×_Y V`, through the identification of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/SmallEtaleChartCorrespondence.lean`.  That identification
makes the sections of the direct image over `V` into homomorphisms out of `chartFiber`, by cover
density of the comparison functor of Stacks 03G1.

`chartFiber` is only a presheaf, so it does not corepresent anything; the sheaf that does is the
subsheaf of the product of copies of `𝒪_X` indexed by the regular functions on `V` generated by
the image of the coordinate map.  The generic construction of that sheaf and of its universal
property is the `Stacks.Sites.sheafOfMono` group of declarations in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/SmallEtaleTwoMorphismRigidity.lean`.
`Stacks.Sites.denseYonedaEquiv` is `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsCoverDense.restrictHomEquivHom`
read as a Yoneda-style description of the sections of a sheaf on the larger site.

